module ImportInnerCommentSortsEitherOrder exposing (v)

-- The same two imports as `ImportInnerAndTrailingMultiline`, written in the
-- OTHER order. Both spellings must format to the same bytes -- the sort is what
-- makes the author's order stop mattering -- and this one did not.
--
-- A comment written INSIDE an import is promoted to a sibling `OriginalRows`
-- whose span STRADDLES the import, so a unit's rows are no longer in row order.
-- `unitLastRow` read only the trailing comments and the import, answering with a
-- row the LEADING comment is still occupying, so `collectRun`'s "the next unit
-- starts on the row right after this one ends" test saw a gap between two
-- adjacent imports and ENDED the run. Nothing sorted across the break, and
-- `VerticalSpace` emitted the blank line the same misreading implies -- which
-- made the wrong grouping stable, so no idempotency check could see it. Only
-- `gen-random.py` v1.38's `sort-order` oracle could, by asking whether the two
-- authorings agree.
--
-- Both row tests had to move together. Correcting only the blank-line pass left
-- `collectRun` still splitting the run: the first format then failed to sort
-- while the second, reading the hoisted comment back at column 1, succeeded.


import {- k1
   bravo -} Foo2 {- k2
   tango -}
import Qux0


v =
    0
